From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: cubie-a7s: mmc aliases so the card indexes stop moving

Without an "mmc" alias the mmc core hands out host indexes in probe order:
mmc_alloc_host() reads of_alias_get_id(dev->of_node, "mmc") and, when there is
none, falls back to the first non-reserved index (drivers/mmc/core/host.c:532,
6.18.36). Probe order is not stable on this board -- the SD card came up as
mmcblk0 on two boots of one kernel and as mmcblk1 on a third, 2026-09-10 --
so every path that names a number is a coin flip, and the board's selftest
already works around it by picking the device through
/sys/block/mmcblkN/device/type instead.

The alias id is the controller index, which is what the node names anyway:

  mmc0 -> mmc@4020000, SMHC0, the SD socket (allwinner,sun60i-a733-mmc)
  mmc2 -> mmc@4022000, SMHC2, the soldered eMMC (allwinner,sun60i-a733-emmc)

Where those two come from: the bases are the UM's (SMHC0 0x04020000, SMHC2 0x04022000). Which controller
carries what is read off the board, not inferred -- 4020000.mmc logs "Got CD
GPIO" and only the SD socket has a card detect, and the eMMC answers on
4022000.mmc, where its EXT_CSD names the part DV4032 (read 2026-09-19).

mmc1 and mmc3 stay unallocated: our DT models SMHC0 and SMHC2 only. Whether
SMHC1's pins (PG0-PG5 at selector 2) go anywhere on this
board is unmeasured -- the WiFi part is not on them, it sits behind the on-board
USB hub (out-of-tree/aic8800/README.md).

This changes only what the numbers are, not what boots: the image's extlinux
entry names root=PARTUUID=... (scripts/stages/image.sh), so nothing in the boot path
reads an mmcblk number.

⚠ Placed late in the series on purpose: the hunk's context is the /aliases node as
`arm64-dts-a733-ethernet0-alias-for-uboot-mac` leaves it (ethernet0 + serial0). That patch
applies well after the eMMC patches such as `arm64-dts-a733-emmc-declare-the-soldered-card`,
so placing this one next to them would break at fuzz 0.
`arm64-dts-a733-uart1-on-pg6-pg7-pinctrl-proof` is placed late for the same reason.

Verified: applies clean at --fuzz=0; the dtb built from the patched tree carries
mmc0 = /soc/mmc@4020000 and mmc2 = /soc/mmc@4022000 (fdtget, local 2026-09-19).
Pending on silicon: three cold boots with the SD at mmcblk0 and the eMMC at
mmcblk2, and an acceptance run.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		ethernet0 = &gmac0;
+		mmc0 = &mmc0;
+		mmc2 = &mmc2;
 		serial0 = &uart0;
 		serial1 = &uart1;
 	};
